  discoveredBy: Bernard Courtois
  description: "Iodine is a chemical element with symbol I and atomic number 53.
    The name is from Greek \u1F30\u03BF\u03B5\u03B9\u03B4\u03AE\u03C2 ioeid\u0113s,
    meaning violet or purple, due to the color of iodine vapor. Iodine and its compounds
    are primarily used in nutrition, and industrially in the production of acetic
    acid and certain polymers."
